# SEO Super Booster (PUBG Hack)

Playbook: `SEO-SUPER-BOOSTER.md` + `src/data/seo-booster.ts`. CI: `npm run generate:seo-assets`, `npm run build`, `node scripts/verify-seo.mjs`.

## Canonical host

- `brand.url` / `CANONICAL_ORIGIN` → `https://pubghack.org` (apex, no `www`).
- `pubghack.org`, `www.pubghack.org`, and other legacy hosts → **301** apex (`src/lib/canonical-origin.ts`, `functions/_middleware.js`, `src/worker.ts`).
- Every page: self-referencing `rel=canonical`, `hreflang=en` + `x-default` on apex URLs.

## Metadata

- One `<h1>`; unique `<title>` and meta description sitewide.
- `og:title` / `og:description` match `<title>` / description.
- Default social image: `/og/home.jpg` (1200×630) with width/height meta tags.
- `rel=image_src` on indexable pages.
- `robots`: `index, follow, max-image-preview:large, max-snippet:-1, max-video-preview:-1`.
- No meta keywords, no SearchAction, no keyword-list JSON-LD.

## Structured data

- Shared `@id` `https://pubghack.org/#product` on home and reviews.
- `Organization` + `WebSite` on every page; `SITE_PURPOSE` + six `knowsAbout` terms in `seo-booster.ts`.
- FAQPage graph on `/faq/` (not duplicated on EN home).

## Intent map

Use `SEO_ROUTE_INTENTS` in `src/data/seo-booster.ts` when writing copy — do not render as keyword blocks.

## Build

```bash
npm run generate:seo-assets
npm run build
node scripts/verify-seo.mjs
```
